test_command=sh tests/roles_test.sh
id=testsuite-01 result=green reason=test "testsuite-01: the flow-fence and structure pins are re-keyed to the de-embedded invocation shape (path-form step-1 reference, path-form release prose, 8 fence lines / no sh fence) with every script-behavior assertion unmodified" in tests/antz-flow_test.sh (suite: pass=53 fail=0 skip=2)
id=testsuite-02 result=green reason=test "testsuite-02: the probe-fence pin re-keys to the step-2 path-form probe reference (loud note, no fence reconstruction) with every probe-behavior assertion unmodified" in tests/orchestrator-status-probe_test.sh (suite: 40 passed 0 failed; the probealign-03 pinned-function list retires test_testharness_02_file_source with a loud note)
id=testsuite-03 result=green reason=test "testsuite-03: the fence-region locator and include-marker guard are reworked to the invocation shape (path refs to existing files, change_pending retire gate) with the derivation assertions unmodified" in tests/orchestrator-skills-block_test.sh (suite: 12 passed 0 failed 2 skipped; assert_include_markers deleted, replaced by assert_invocation_lines + compute_permitted_regions)
id=testsuite-04 result=green reason=test "testsuite-04: sessionguards-03's include-marker counts re-key to path-reference invocation lines (no marker anywhere, exactly the three scripts on disk) and orchprose-01's structural counts move to 8 fence lines / 4 blocks / no sh fence" in tests/orchestrator-sessionguards_test.sh (suite: 8 passed 0 failed 1 skipped)
id=testsuite-05 result=green reason=test "testsuite-05: the renderinject suite re-keyed -- retired injection helpers uncalled, renders hermetic, prompt surface invocation-only" in tests/renderinject_test.sh (suite: pass=13 fail=0 skip=1). The re-key: reconstruct_expected_body and assert_no_marker_in_tree retired with loud notes; assert_no_embed_survivor (no marker AND no ```sh script fence in any rendered file) replaces the no-survivor clause; -03's usage pins re-key to the concrete-path invocation forms and the install inventory 12 -> 16 (four libdir scripts); -04's fetch_file pin re-keys to the libdir script fetches; -05's set-model byte-identity masks retire with a loud note (sub-spec 03 legitimately changed those bodies), the marker-3 pin re-keys to marker-0 + injection-machinery-gone, and the --check clause re-keys to base-report + exactly four script lines; -07 re-keys to sub-spec 04's installed-library wording (stale injection/temp-file wordings asserted absent); every render/--check run masks XDG_CONFIG_HOME into the temp home (hermetic); the one-sided dequote_description normalization (fitting a pre-quoting base era only; the merge-base is post-quoting 4.7.1) is fixed to era-neutral norm_render on BOTH sides, clearing the fabricated antz-specifier.md drift
id=testsuite-06 result=green reason=test "testsuite-06: the invocation-form hard constraints re-keyed, the retired tempfile-argument form gone from non-comment lines, and the verifier-02 frozen guard split to scripts+meta" in tests/roles_test.sh (suite: 12 passed 0 failed). terminology-01's state pin re-keys to 'state <slug> "__ANTZ_SCRIPTS_DIR__/antz-probe.sh"', the ensure/release pins keep matching the unchanged subcommand forms, every machine-line constraint (delegation-header lines, probe subspec= line, receipt grammar, closing-block grammar, stop-state tokens) passes unmodified; verifier-02's byte-frozen guard splits to scripts/orchestration/ + agents/meta/ (install.sh retires with a loud note -- this change edits it); terminology-03's access-model cascade cleared by the testsuite-08 repairs
id=testsuite-07 result=green reason=test "testsuite-07: the drift guard compares installed files against sources -- fence-extraction and the skills carve-out are gone" in tests/orchestrator-render-sync_test.sh (suite: 3 passed 0 failed). testharness-04 rewritten: each installed libdir script equals its scripts/orchestration/ source byte-for-byte after stripping the single inserted marker line (plus source+marker line-count, shebang, and marker-position checks); the drift half still works -- tampering one byte of the installed antz-probe.sh reports exactly antz-probe out of sync; the render-side fence walkers (extract_fences/expected_block) and the antz-skills.sh under-fence-indent carve-out are gone
id=testsuite-08 result=green reason=test "testsuite-08: the repo's full unit suite runs green with ids reported; no script content survives in prompts, renders, or extractor call sites" in tests/roles_test.sh (recursion-guarded: an invocation inside another glob returns early; roles_test.sh and description-quoting_test.sh -- the other glob-runner -- excluded from the inner loop; the outer direct runs prove both green). All 38 tests/*_test.sh exit 0 and report scenario ids. Documented de-embed-era repairs to suites not named by sub-specs 01/03/05 (they could NOT pass unmodified; each is minimal): tests/sluglimit_test.sh step1_window re-keys from the removed step-1 embed's fenced window to the heading form (1. **Derive / 2. **Probe, same extractor as the re-keyed prose pins; the gated working-vs-HEAD window guards untouched); tests/access-model_test.sh render_tree runs hermetic (env -u XDG_CONFIG_HOME -- the libdir step was writing to the REAL ~/.config/antz) and render-03 masks each side's temp-home path to a token before the cross-home byte cmp (the de-embedded body legitimately embeds the resolved libdir, so a raw cross-home cmp would attribute the path to the meta; the masking is a no-op on path-free bodies); tests/skills-activation-render_test.sh gets the same hermetic render_to and the same home-path mask on its cross-home comparisons (render-03, render-04 determinism, render-04-scoping else branch); tests/description-quoting_test.sh quoting-05's static renderinject needle re-keys from the retired reconstruction call to the loud re-key note + norm_render; renderinject's own dequote asymmetry fix (under testsuite-05) cleared quoting-05's dynamic half. No-extraction clause proven mechanically: zero markers and zero ```sh fences in all four prompts, zero markers/fences in every rendered file of a fresh hermetic render, and the extraction-era idioms (marker-substitution rebuild, assert_no_marker_in_tree, extract_fences, expected_block) appear in no suite's non-comment lines -- invocations_test.sh's same-named reconstruct helper is the inverted prompt+substitution oracle and survives the scan by design. Deviations: (1) the "pass unmodified" clause is met only via the five listed minimal repairs (the suites were red on arrival from sub-specs 01-03's legitimate render/shape changes); (2) the testsuite-08 test lives in roles_test.sh (the feature names no home for it; roles_test.sh is the cross-cutting prompt/role hub and its testsuite-06 line sits beside it); (3) the suite's own e2e-01 skip stub (archived orchestrator-fast-path scenario) keeps its historical wording -- verifier-owned territory
